
### 1. Data we collect
**We do not collect your name, email, phone number, or any other directly-identifying information.** 
The App has no account system and no login.

| Data | Purpose | Collected by |
|---|---|---|
| App usage events (level starts/completions, hint usage, purchases, ad views) | Understand which parts of the game are used, fix balance issues | Firebase Analytics (Google) |
| Crash reports and error logs | Fix bugs | Firebase Crashlytics (Google) |
| Advertising identifier (IDFA on iOS, Android Advertising ID on Android) and other device/ad-interaction data | Show ads, measure ad performance; may be used by our ad partner for personalized advertising if you allow tracking | Google AdMob, and AdMob's own mediated ad networks |
| Purchase receipts | Process the one-time "Remove Ads" purchase and let you restore it on a new device | Apple App Store / Google Play billing |

_If a new third-party service is ever added, add a row here._

### 2. Data stored only on your device

Your coin balance, level progress, purchased cosmetics, daily streak, and
settings (sound/haptics) are stored locally on your device only. This
data is not sent to us and is deleted if you uninstall the App. There is
currently no cloud save or cross-device sync.

### 3. Advertising and tracking

The App shows ads (interstitial between levels, and optional
"watch a video" ads you choose to view in exchange for an in-game hint,
undo, extra move, or streak recovery) served through **Google AdMob**.
AdMob may work with third-party ad networks that set their own cookies or
device identifiers.

**On iOS**, the first time this matters the App shows Apple's App Tracking
Transparency prompt and asks your permission before using the advertising
identifier for personalized ads. If you decline, you'll still see ads,
just not ones personalized to your interests.

**On Android**, ads may use the Android Advertising ID unless you've
opted out of ad personalization in your device's Google Settings.

You can review Google's own privacy practices for AdMob at
https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads.

### 4. In-app purchases

The App offers one purchase, "Remove Ads." Payment is processed entirely
by Apple or Google — we never see or store your payment card details.

### 5. Children's privacy

The App is a general-audience casual puzzle game and is not directed at
children under 13 (or the relevant age of consent in your country). We do
not knowingly collect personal information from children. [If you intend
to market this app toward children, or expect a substantial child
audience, you must revisit this section together with Google Play's
Families Policy and the FTC's COPPA rule — that changes what ad
personalization and analytics are allowed and is out of scope of this
draft.]

### 6. Data retention and deletion

Analytics and crash data are retained by Firebase per Google's standard
retention settings. Since the App has no account system, there's no
"delete my account" action — uninstalling the App removes all
locally-stored data, and you can request deletion of any analytics data
tied to your device by contacting us at [support email] with your
device's advertising identifier.

### 7. Your choices

- **Ad personalization**: controlled by your OS-level setting (iOS App
  Tracking Transparency, Android "Opt out of Ads Personalization").
- **Remove ads entirely**: the in-app "Remove Ads" purchase removes
  interstitial ads (rewarded video, which you opt into per-use, stays
  available since it's your choice, not an interruption).

### 8. Changes to this policy

We may update this policy as the App changes. Material changes will be
reflected by updating the effective date above.

